# ProjectHelioTrip

## Stack
- Vite + React 19 + TypeScript (strict).
- 3D: three, @react-three/fiber, @react-three/drei.
- State: zustand (no Context for global state).
- Icons: lucide-react.

## Structure
- `src/components/` – UI components.
- `src/scene/` – R3F components (Canvas content).
- `src/store/` – zustand stores.
- `src/hooks/` – custom hooks.
- `src/lib/` – framework-agnostic helpers.

## Filenames & exports
- `PascalCase.tsx` for components, `camelCase.ts` for everything else.
- Named exports for components – no default exports.
- One component per file.

## Code style
- Early return over deep nesting.
- No comments that only repeat the code.
- No dead code or unused imports.
- Performance matters: avoid unnecessary allocation, memoize heavy work.

## CI / Vercel
- Production build uses `tsc` with `noUnusedLocals` / `noUnusedParameters` (see `tsconfig`). Unused imports, props, or destructured values **fail the build**.
- Before claiming a task is done, run `npm run build` (or at least `npx tsc --noEmit`) and fix all TS errors. Do not leave placeholder props “for later” on components.

## Communication
- If the agent asked a question and got no answer, ask again before continuing work.
